Addressed. Fixed in commit 45e2471.

`_tick_names` now parses the list shape:
```python
def _tick_names(path: Path) -> set[str]:
    try:
        data = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) or []
        if isinstance(data, list):
            return {e["name"] for e in data if isinstance(e, dict) and "name" in e}
    except Exception:
        pass
    return set()
```

All four test fixtures rebuilt with the real `[{"name": ...}]` format. Also added `test_scheduler_delta_bundled_template_is_list_parseable` which round-trips the actual `mimir/scheduler_template.yaml` — schema can't silently drift again.

31/31 tests pass.

Re: 🟠 `_env_gaps` timing issue — reads pre-`execv` stale builtin-skills while docstring claims otherwise. Will address in a follow-up so this PR ships the blocking fixes cleanly.
